{
 "about": "End-to-end encryption: envelopes made by the link client (ade_link.py) from fixed keys and nonces, for the page to open and refuse as the Python tests do. Keys are base64url without padding; private keys raw (32 bytes) and, for the content key, as PKCS#8 DER too; plaintext_text is the plaintext's RFC 8785 bytes as text. A talk's i counts from 0. The page's own sealed vectors go in e2e_v1_page.json, in this file's shape (content_key, envelopes with slot, plaintext and envelope), which the Python tests open when it is there. The grant seals the master key's 32 bytes as they are (the envelope's construction, its AAD the grant's); the content-key wrap is AES-256-GCM under the content-wrap subkey, given as nonce, wrapped (ciphertext and tag) and the two together.",
